# Public API (cm:*)
  @api cm:setContext(newTake)  @ 428-433
      @contract  setContext(nil) clears take+track; setContext(take) derives track via GetMediaItemTrack  @ 426
      @contract  refreshes all persisted caches (transient resets to {}) and fires configChanged {}  @ 427
  @api cm:clearTake()  @ 435-440
  @api cm:boundTake()  @ 443
      @contract  bound take pointer; nil when context is cleared (take/track tiers resolve off empty)  @ 442
  @api cm:boundTrack()  @ 446
      @contract  bound track pointer; nil when context is cleared (track tier resolves off empty)  @ 445
  @api cm:setTrack(newTrack)  @ 448-453
  @api cm:pollUndo()  @ 456
      @contract  delegates to the engine watcher; cm's watch group reloads tiers and fires configChanged  @ 455
  @api cm:isDeclared(key)  @ 493
      @contract  non-raising existence test against the schema; true iff key is declared  @ 492
  @api cm:get(key, opts)  @ 500-507
      -- pick is orthogonal to the merge mode: it indexes whatever that mode resolved, so only the
      -- one entry crosses the boundary. A nil pick is indistinguishable from none (see the spec).
  @api cm:getAt(level, key)  @ 510-519
      @contract  reads single tier only (no merge, no defaults); key nil → whole-cache clone  @ 509
  @api cm:valueFor(handle, scope, key)  @ 522-529
      @contract  single-tier value for a foreign take/track handle (ps:getAt); no merge or defaults  @ 521
  @api cm:defaultFor(key)  @ 532-535
      @contract  deep-copy of the schema default for key (no tiers, no merge); raises on unknown key  @ 531
  -- Writing
  @api cm:set(level, key, value)  @ 540-550
      @contract  deep-copies value into tier cache, persists, fires targeted configChanged  @ 539
  @api cm:remove(level, key)  @ 553-564
      @contract  removes key from named tier; no-op (no signal) if that tier's cache is unloaded  @ 552
  @api cm:assign(level, updates)  @ 567-581
      @contract  validates all keys before any write (all-or-nothing); REMOVE deletes; fires signal  @ 566

